  "all_ingredients_flat": "Tofu, Black pepper powder, Red chilli powder, Turmeric powder, Garam Masala, Cumin powder, Coriander powder, Lemon, Chickpea flour (besan), Red Ragi Upma Rava, Brown Rice Powder, Baking soda, Sumac powder, Garlic powder, Onion powder, Water, Soy yogurt, Carom seeds (ajwain), Himalayan salt",
  "instructions": "For Masala Marinade: Mix black pepper powder (1/2 tsp), red chilli powder (1 tsp), turmeric powder (1/4 tsp), garam masala (1 tsp), cumin powder (1 tsp), coriander powder (1/2 tsp), and freshly squeezed lemon (1 Tbsp) into a thick paste.\nFor Chickpea Batter: Mix chickpea flour (besan) (1/3 cup), Red Ragi Upma Rava (1.5 Tbsp, Brown Rice Powder will do too), black pepper powder (1 tsp), red chilli powder (1.5 tsp), turmeric powder (1/4 tsp), garam masala powder (1.5 tsp), cumin powder (1 tsp), baking soda (a pinch), sumac powder (1 tsp), garlic powder (1 tsp), onion powder (1 tsp), water or soy yogurt (1/4 cup, adjust quantity if batter is thick, I used water), carom seeds (ajwain) (1/2 tsp), and optional Himalayan salt into a thick paste.\nTo make Tofu Pakoda: Take two 1/2 inch slices of tofu. Drain the water using Tofu Press. Wrap tofu in cheese cloth and place a heavy object on it for 3-4 hours. Make 2-3 criss cross cuts on tofu slices. Cover them generously with Masala Marinade. Set aside for 20-25 minutes for marination. Dip marinated tofu slices in Chickpea Batter. Apply the batter on both sides, covering the slices fully. Preheat the air fryer at 350 F. The air fryer container must be warm before we place Tofu Pakodas in it. Place Tofu Pakodas in the air fryer. Turn them over after 8 minutes. If the Pakodas is sticking to the bottom then cook for another minute before turning over. Cook for another 8-10 minutes. Turn them over. Pakodas should feel crisp to the touch. Let them sit for 5-10 minutes.",
  "cooking_methods": [
    "no-cook",
    "air-fry"
  ],
  "serving_suggestion": "Enjoy with any chutneys of your choice!",
  "notes": "A recipe with WHOLE GRAINS (Red Ragi Upma Rava | Brown Rice Powder), BEANS (tofu, chickpea flour), LIME-LEMON-VINEGAR (lemon), HERBS & SPICES (various). Sub-recipes: Masala Marinade, Chickpea Batter.",
